118:  *   It's better to extend features via plugins, instead of enabling HTML.
119:  * - __xhtmlOut__ - `false`. Set `true` to add '/' when closing single tags
120:  *   (`<br />`). This is needed only for full CommonMark compatibility. In real
121:  *   world you will need HTML output.
122:  * - __breaks__ - `false`. Set `true` to convert `\n` in paragraphs into `<br>`.
123:  * - __langPrefix__ - `language-`. CSS language class prefix for fenced blocks.
124:  *   Can be useful for external highlighters.
125:  * - __linkify__ - `false`. Set `true` to autoconvert URL-like text to links.
126:  * - __typographer__  - `false`. Set `true` to enable [some language-neutral
127:  *   replacement](https://github.com/markdown-it/markdown-it/blob/master/lib/rules_core/replacements.js) +
128:  *   quotes beautification (smartquotes).
129:  * - __quotes__ - `“”‘’`, string. Double + single quotes replacement pairs, when
130:  *   typographer enabled and smartquotes on. Set doubles to '«»' for Russian,
131:  *   '„“' for German.
132:  * - __highlight__ - `null`. Highlighter function for fenced code blocks.
